<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15307" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕgēnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		egeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>in want of</i>, <i>in need of</i>, <i>destitute</i> or <i>void of</i> any
			thing (rare, and mostly <b>poet.</b> for egens).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(nos) omnium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 1, 599</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv.
				9, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis spei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquarum (regio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 15, 3</span></i>
			
			<i>fin.</i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4,
			30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					6, 304</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With abl.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">commeatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 12, 46</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">15, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				i. e. <i>indigent</i>, <i>needy</i>,
					<i>necessitous</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 2, 3, 46</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Poen. 1, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 6,
				91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 365</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 367</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frater,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Deut. 15, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Poor</i>, <i>worthless</i>, <i>beggarly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad infirma et egena elementa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gal. 4, 9</span></i>
			. —Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕgēnus</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>a poor
			man</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et pauper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 34, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Sir. 4, 4 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕgēnum</span></b> ,
				i, n., <i>a poor
			soil</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in egeno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 10, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 31,
		1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
